{ instr_mnemonic.init - a DSEE derived object of be_com/opcodes.def
  (cc.a88k only), which the opcode generator made with
  opcode_enumeration.ins.pas: the initializer of the section
  instruction_mnemonic (0x2B7A3C: 384 entries of 12 characters, the
  opcodes' names without the OPC$ prefix, "********" for 0).  Included
  by lst.pas after the opcode enumeration.

  No Apollo copy survives; reconstructed from the DOMAIN C 6.9 binary
  cc.a88k, the section's bytes (every entry agrees with the opcode
  enumeration's identifier of its ordinal: `tools/cc_enumnames.py
  ctape/.../cc.a88k 0x209FEE').

  How the section is shared (docs/questions.md 161, settled by
  translator PB2): backend.ins.pas declares the section's variable for
  every unit (`var (instruction_mnemonic) instruction_mnemonic: ...'); this file, included by
  the one unit that holds the data, gives it its initial value with a
  `define' statement (the language reference's section 7.2.2, method 2:
  a define statement after the var declaration, "useful ... when you
  write an %include file").  dpc lays the defined variable out in the
  named section with its data.

  Not known from the original: the file's layout. }

